# Unit 3: Building Data-Driven Systems with AI - Overview

## What is Building Data-Driven Systems with AI all about?
 
#### In **Building Data-Driven Systems**, students expand their skills as developers by creating web apps that organize, display, and manipulate meaningful datasets.

#### Through schema-informed design and hands-on coding with arrays and objects, they learn to treat data as both a design material and a responsibility, building features that are reliable, ethical, and user-focused.

---

#### ***Note: Unlike the first semester, the second semester of AI Foundations is a continuous sequence and must be taught in order. Building Data-Driven Systems is the 3rd unit in the course.***

## Student Learning Goals
<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; background: #f7f8fa; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); font-size: 14pt; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 800px; margin: 20px auto;">

  <div>
    <h4 style="margin-top: 0; font-weight: bold;">By the end of this unit, students will be able to :</h4>
    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14pt">
      <li>Represent real-world information using arrays and objects, designing simple schemas that define the fields, data types, and constraints of their datasets.

</li> <br>
      <li>Build web app features that display and update data.</li><br>
      <li>Use AI-generated scaffolds for data choices and program behavior.
</li><br>
      <li>Combine arrays and objects to manage collections of data, writing functions that retrieve, modify, filter, search, and sort information.
</li><br>
<li>Apply data-structure skills in a meaningful final project.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
